P11Lab-authored for the sc-hsm provider recipe: store only the terminal
CA certificate in EF_TERMCA (FID 2F02, C.DevAut).

The INITIALIZE handler builds two objects back to back in one output
buffer: the 0x67-wrapped device authentication object (ee_len bytes at
res_APDU for EF_EE_DEV) and the bare terminal CA CVC (term_len bytes
at res_APDU + ee_len). It then stores EF_TERMCA from res_APDU with
length ee_len + term_len, i.e. the authentication object concatenated
with the CA certificate.

No consumer expects that layout. CardContact's libsc-hsm-pkcs11
(token-sc-hsm.c decodeDevAutCert) parses EF_TERMCA as one CVC
optionally followed by the issuer CA CVC and refuses the token when
the leading tag is not 0x7f21 ("Error not a certificate"); the
firmware's own reset_puk_store/cvc_get_chr and XKEK domain creation
(cvc_get_pub over EF_TERMCA) likewise expect a CVC at offset 0.
Current upstream pico-hsm master writes a bare CVC here (verified
natively: 443-byte 7f21 object), as did the 2023 firmware that
generated the in-tree tests/memory.tar.gz fixture (CVC pair).

Store res_APDU + ee_len with length term_len so EF_TERMCA holds
exactly the generated terminal CA CVC. Simulation-fidelity fix,
declared in the recipe locks and notices; without it a freshly
initialized card presents no token to the module under test.

Upstream: https://github.com/polhenarejos/pico-hsm.git at
251b35dd9c4fd929923fc3b192f6793826efeaef (v6.6).

--- a/src/hsm/cmd_initialize.c
+++ b/src/hsm/cmd_initialize.c
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@
             }
             mbedtls_ecdsa_free(&ecdsa);
             fpk = search_file(EF_TERMCA);
-            ret = file_put_data(fpk, res_APDU, ee_len + term_len);
+            /* P11Lab: EF_TERMCA holds the bare terminal CA CVC only. */
+            ret = file_put_data(fpk, res_APDU + ee_len, term_len);
             if (ret != 0) {
                 return SW_EXEC_ERROR();
             }
